            \},\
            "rating": 2,\
            "description": "I rarely leave bad reviews, as I don't want to have a negative effect on a business based on what could just be one bad day. By the food here is terrible, and I simply can't understand how they've been in business this long. I got all basic things in a take out order, pupu platter, general tsos, egg rolls. The general tsos was batered so heavy is was near inedible, and there was next to no sauce. At some places it comes swimming in sauce and that's its own kind of bad, but skimpy sauce is worse. My partner theorized the chicken was frozen pre battered from a bag, and I think she's right. In the platter, the Crab Rangoon had hardly any filling, the shrimp-toast was just pieces of fried shrimp, maybe they ran out idk, and everything was super greasy. Heavy, old fryer oil flavor that coats your tongue and upsets your stomach. Oh and got the Singapore noodles, they forgot the curry. Plain, completely unseasoned noodles and a few veggies, absolutely nothing someone would knowing order or want to even eat, and someone, knowing fully well the orders not right because the noodles arent yellow from curry, boxed it up and put it in the bag anyway. Luckily i had some curry powder in the cabinet. The egg roll was good, that's honest to God the only positive of the whole meal. All of this was not indicative of a \\"Bad Day\\", their sub-mediocrity is deeply entrenched.\\nI did something I've never done with Chinese takeout; I immediately threw away the copious leftovers. Easily the worst Chinese I've ever had, and I'm not comparing this to the really good China town spots I've been to all over, but just run of the mill, strip mall take out Chinese.",\
